<section vertical-align="center" id="bbs010" image-layout="blank"><card-template-instructions>Three unranked peers in subtle boxes under one working title, each led by an icon chip on the box edge with a short title and one or two sentences; every cell the same shape.</card-template-instructions><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="a89YsDjmdd"><h2>Priorities for the next two quarters</h2><grid padding-top="48pt" spacing="medium" marker-straddle="true" marker-align="center" marker-position="above" marker-shape="circle" marker-style="solid" marker-size="large" marker="icon"><grid-item colspan="20" cell-style="subtle" id="wtIRsTkYoH"><grid-item-label><icon alt="repeat order cycle" source="image.pictographic.icon" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/FJU4auuHQNo32uoq9saFe7.svg?stroke=45"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Keep repeat customers</h3><p>Move every account with two or more orders onto a standing schedule with a named contact.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="20" cell-style="subtle" id="2i3iVnLVVR"><grid-item-label><icon alt="product launch checklist" source="image.pictographic.icon" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Em0QCBefA64jPxWdRJ8H.svg?stroke=45"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Finish the new lines</h3><p>Ship training material and pricing for both lines before the autumn sales cycle begins.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="20" cell-style="subtle" id="_JUnLUoJqT"><grid-item-label><icon alt="warehouse capacity" source="image.pictographic.icon" src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/xlYAb3XwZz5FJWPrFtU9.svg?stroke=45"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Recover capacity</h3><p>Bring the second warehouse shift back and hold two weeks of stock on the top twenty items.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>